   {
    "text": "In 1752, Britain went to bed on Wednesday, September second.",
    "who": "CS"
   },
   {
    "text": "And woke up on Thursday, September fourteenth?",
    "who": "RR"
   },
   {
    "text": "Eleven days, gone. On purpose.",
    "who": "CS"
   },
   {
    "text": "Why would anyone do that?",
    "who": "RR"
   },
   {
    "text": "The old calendar ran about eleven minutes long every year. By 1752, it was eleven days off.",
    "who": "CS"
   },
   {
    "text": "Even George Washington's birthday moved, from February eleventh to February twenty-second.",
    "who": "CS"
   },
   {
    "text": "History makes no sense. Follow for more.",
    "who": "RR"
   }
